# Dhriti and the Curious Elephant with the Banana

One quiet evening, Dhriti was sitting with Mamma and Dada.

The sky was soft and pink.

The birds were going home.

It was a calm time.

Near the garden lived a little elephant named Ebu.

Ebu loved bananas.

Big bananas.

Small bananas.

Yellow bananas.

Ebu loved them all.

One day, Ebu found a very special banana.

It was shiny and golden.

"Oh!" said Ebu.

"Where did this banana come from?"

Ebu was curious.

Very curious.

He looked under a tree.

No answer.

He looked near the flowers.

No answer.

He looked beside a little pond.

Still no answer.

Dhriti watched Ebu.

Dhriti smiled.

"Keep looking, Ebu," said Dhriti.

Ebu nodded.

He kept looking.

He kept wondering.

He kept asking.

Soon, Ebu saw a tiny trail of banana peels.

One peel.

Two peels.

Three peels.

"Interesting!" said Ebu.

He followed the trail slowly.

Step by step.

Step by step.

Dhriti walked with Mamma and Dada nearby.

Everyone stayed together.

The trail led to a small banana plant.

There were many bananas there.

Big bananas.

Small bananas.

Yellow bananas.

Just like Ebu liked.

Then Ebu understood.

A strong wind had gently moved one banana from the plant.

That was the shiny banana he found.

"Oh!" laughed Ebu.

"Now I know!"

Dhriti clapped.

Mamma smiled.

Dada smiled.

Ebu was happy.

Not because he found a banana.

But because he learned something new.

The sky became darker.

The stars began to twinkle.

Ebu ate a small banana.

Dhriti waved goodbye.

"Good night, Ebu."

"Good night, Dhriti," said Ebu.

The garden was quiet.

The stars were bright.

Dhriti sat close to Mamma and Dada.

Everything felt warm.

Everything felt calm.

And soon, it was time for sleep.

Good night, Dhriti.

Good night, little elephant.

Good night, stars.
